WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.650
There are shortcuts that give you your distance off a light with no plotting at all, just a watch.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.775
The easiest is the bow and beam bearing.

3
00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:10.850
Look at the diagram.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.975
Note the time when the light is forty-five degrees off your bow.

5
00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:17.275
Hold your course and speed.

6
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:21.700
Note the time again when it’s abeam, ninety degrees off the bow.

7
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.025
Work out how far you ran between the two times.

8
00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:29.575
That distance equals your distance off the light when it was abeam.

9
00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:32.200
Why does it work?

10
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:33.825
Draw it.

11
00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:36.625
Forty-five degrees, then ninety.

12
00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:40.025
That’s a right triangle with two equal sides.

13
00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:42.925
One side is the distance you ran.

14
00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:45.400
The other is your distance off.

15
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.350
They’re the same.

16
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.850
So next time you pass a lighthouse, try it, and check the answer against your plotter.
